{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013a1JYx16CCC11aTXptdF8P","type":"tool_result","content":"17:    inference_profiles:{ o:{ protocol:'chat', model:'m' } },\n60:test('doctor keeps all local checks after missing or invalid config',\n94:test('doctor checks gate health and only user-level skill installations',\n145:test('doctor inspects both stored scopes even with an environment key',\n184:test('doctor never echoes malformed credential JSON', async t => {\n198:test('doctor requires clone approval for custom endpoints', async t => {\n206:                protocol:'chat',\n229:test('doctor diagnoses proxy variables without exposing the URL', async t => {\n253:test('doctor probes models with each role protocol and no key in output',\n262:        for (const protocol of ['chat', 'responses', 'anthropic']) {\n269:                            protocol,\n277:            t.equal(res.code, 0, `${protocol} adapter is available`)\n303:                    protocol === 'anthropic' ? undefined : `Bearer ${key}`,\n304:                    'bearer authentication for OpenAI protocols')\n306:                    protocol === 'anthropic' ? key : undefined,\n308:                t.equal(req.headers['anthropic-version'],\n309:                    protocol === 'anthropic' ? '2023-06-01' : undefined,\n319:test('doctor classifies models status without disclosing response bodies',\n349:test('doctor refuses redirects without sending the key to their target',\n370:test('doctor bounds a models request to five seconds and continues',\n392:test('doctor withholds ambient keys from a custom finder independently',\n403:                direct:{ model:'m', protocol:'anthropic' },\n424:            res.hosts.every(h => h === 'api.anthropic.com'),\n432:test('doctor reports stored credential scopes through role resolution',\n462:test('doctor skips invalid profiles while retaining later diagnostics',\n490:test('doctor makes no requests until custom endpoint trust is current',\n500:                o:{ protocol:'chat', model:'m', endpoint:server.url + '/v1' },\n538:test('doctor bounds models body reads and hides reflected credentials',\n563:test('doctor chat roundtrip uses two turns with a stable prefix', async t => {\n583:test('doctor rejects a guessed token without doctor_lookup', async t => {\n599:test('doctor rejects a changed lookup token on the final turn', async t => {\n616:test('doctor sends the configured session header on both chat turns',\n623:                    protocol:'chat',\n646:test('doctor emits approved chat diagnostics for an explicit config',\n657:                o:{ protocol:'chat', model:'m', api_key_env:'DOCTOR_KEY' },\nad08ceb Merge responses adapter (ticket 27) into anthropic adapter (ticket 28)\n2b18f0c doctor tests: anthropic roundtrip now available; probe fake speaks anthropic\nb4a4e6f llm: dispatch the responses protocol; adapter-seam tests\nc429f3e Cover approved doctor chat config and credential reporting\n7b71ef2 Cover doctor session headers across both probe turns\nc6a69f3 Require doctor lookup token to roundtrip\n4d39d5d Add doctor chat two-turn roundtrip probe\n7557753 Verify bounded doctor responses and complete validation\nissues/\nlearnings.md\nlogs/\nprogress.md\nreview.md\nspec/\nspec.md\n   `<role>-profile`, `<role>-endpoint`, `<role>-roundtrip`\n6. Local checks: `git`, `git-gate`, `project-credentials`,\n   `user-credentials`, `proxy-env`, then one `<harness>-skill` per\n   user-level skill target (or a single `agent-skills`).\n\nEarly exits: if `config-file` or `config` fails, steps after it up to 5\nare skipped and the local checks (6) still run. Within step 5 the rules\nbelow decide which per-role checks appear.\n\n#### `build`\n\n- Uses the shared build info (CLI core area). esbuild injects version,\n  commit, and build date through `define` at build time; running from\n  source reports version `dev`, so the development-build warning below\n  still applies. Its one-line string, Go `buildinfo.String()`, is\n  `\"<v> (commit <c>)\"` when the version is the sentinel `dev` or the\n  date is unknown, else `\"<v> (<commit>, <date>)\"`.\n- `warn` with detail `<string>; development build` when the version is the\n  development sentinel `dev`; otherwise `pass` with detail `<string>`.\n\n#### `config-file`\n\n- With `--config <path>`: that path is used as given (no existence check\n  here; a missing file fails the `config` check). `pass`, detail = path.\n- Without `--config`: search with the config area's `find(cwd, stop)`,\n  where `stop` is the Git toplevel of cwd, or cwd itself outside a\n  repository.\n  - Search error -> `fail`, detail = error message.\n  - Nothing found -> `fail`, detail = the shared \"no project config\"\n    message: `no project config (.roast.json) found between here and the\n    Git toplevel; run \\`npx roast init\\` to create one`.\n6. `<role>-endpoint`, then `<role>-roundtrip` (both always run when\n   trusted; a failed endpoint check does not skip the roundtrip).\n\n#### `<role>-endpoint` (models listing probe)\n\n- URL: `baseURL` with trailing `/` characters removed, plus `/models`.\n  If it does not parse as an absolute request URI -> `fail`,\n  `invalid models endpoint: <err>`.\n- `GET` with a 5 second timeout (per request; Go also gives the client a\n  5 second timeout). Headers: for protocol `anthropic`,\n  `x-api-key: <key>` and `anthropic-version: 2023-06-01`; for every other\n  protocol, `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. No session header, no other\n  headers.\n- Read and discard at most 32 KiB of the body.\n- Results:\n  - transport error -> `fail`, `GET <url>: <err>`\n  - 2xx -> `pass`, `GET <url>: HTTP <status>` (Go prints the status line,\n    e.g. `200 OK`)\n  - 401 or 403 -> `fail`, `credential rejected by <url>: HTTP <status>`\n  - >= 500 -> `fail`, `<url> returned HTTP <status>`\n  - anything else (e.g. 404, 3xx, 429) -> `warn`,\n    `endpoint is reachable but model listing returned HTTP <status>`\n\n#### `<role>-roundtrip` (two-turn tool probe)\n\nExercises what a review relies on: a tool call, its result replayed on the\nnext request, and a final submission on the reserved wrap-up turn, all\nunder automatic tool choice with an unchanged conversation prefix. A\nsingle-call probe passes on routes that then fail every review.\n\n- Max output tokens: the role's value if in `1..512`, else `512`.\n- The roundtrip uses the LLM area's client and agent loop with\n  `AbortSignal.timeout(35_000)` combined with the command signal.\n- Status text: Node `fetch` gives `status` and `statusText`; render\n  `HTTP ${status} ${statusText}`.trim (statusText may be empty on HTTP/2).\n- Depends on: config (`find`, `load`, `resolveRole`, `validateRole`,\n  credential description, trust projection), credentials (paths, `load`,\n  `withStoredCredentials`), trust (`approved`), scope (`gitRoot`), gate\n  (`inspect`, `summary`, `active`), skill (`installationTargets`,\n  `inspect`), llm (client, converse, `AuthError`), CLI core (build info,\n  error/exit mapping).\n\n### `src/cli/init.ts`\n\n```ts\nexport function writeStarter (\n    cwd:string,\n    finderModel:string,\n    verifierModel:string","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8db26e43-7bde-47a9-88ba-95dcb38ede5e","uuid":"88945294-dc98-4eb4-822e-59ed292d50c7","timestamp":"2026-11-24T03:37:39.809Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"17:    inference_profiles:{ o:{ protocol:'chat', model:'m' } },\n60:test('doctor keeps all local checks after missing or invalid config',\n94:test('doctor checks gate health and only user-level skill installations',\n145:test('doctor inspects both stored scopes even with an environment key',\n184:test('doctor never echoes malformed credential JSON', async t => {\n198:test('doctor requires clone approval for custom endpoints', async t => {\n206:                protocol:'chat',\n229:test('doctor diagnoses proxy variables without exposing the URL', async t => {\n253:test('doctor probes models with each role pro